--- R21 DECISION: accepted credential (:15) and PAT scopes (:23) ---
R21 DECISION sha256=66d566a55330e2417a2e5227bcac64e3312fc56280db09d7b74a13425aa346c1
    15	**The contributors-bot workflow keeps GitHub App credentials as the primary credential and sources its `pat:` fallback from a dedicated repository secret, `CONTRIBUTORS_PLEASE_PAT`, holding a fine-grained personal access token scoped to the single repository. This is `py-launch-blueprint`'s shape. `ts-launch-blueprint`'s `pat: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}` is not adopted.** The action is `smorinlabs/contributors-please-action` at tag `v1.3.9` = commit `3c6dbff9ef21190aa1f63b3c400ed4f0ab404ac1` (resolved locally in this run, `review/evidence/contributors-bot-credential-source.log` case 01), which both source repos already run in `mode: pull-request` under ledger row F060. The ranked runner-up is App-credentials-only with no `pat:` input at all.
    23	| F061 Contributors-bot credential source for the PAT fallback | `pat: ${{ secrets.CONTRIBUTORS_PLEASE_PAT }}` — a dedicated repository secret holding a fine-grained PAT (Contents: write, Pull requests: write, Issues: write, single repository, explicit expiry), used only when `app-id` and `private-key` are absent; documented as an either/or with the App path, never as a third required secret |
